201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (An analogy that resonates here is the difference between a well-designed vending machine and a skilled chef. The vending machine can deliver predictable outputs based on predefined inputs. But a chef learns your tastes, adapts to new ingredients, and improves over time. LLMs have the potential to be the latter but only if we give them the right kitchen, ingredients, and feedback.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
